1
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:29,760
Nakarai.

2
00:00:33,410 --> 00:00:35,020
What's that?

3
00:00:35,710 --> 00:00:37,110
A penguin.

4
00:00:37,110 --> 00:00:39,300
As a thank-you for the watermelon.

5
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:52,080
Is this how you get in?

6
00:00:52,080 --> 00:00:54,560
Yeah, a bit further that way.

7
00:01:01,810 --> 00:01:04,000
Whoa.

8
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,970
Don't just watch.

9
00:01:05,970 --> 00:01:08,560
You're making me do everything.

10
00:01:09,180 --> 00:01:11,880
It doesn't match my personality.

11
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:14,180
Same here, you know?

12
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:16,938
All right.

13
00:01:17,830 --> 00:01:19,720
I'm doing double syrup.

14
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:21,800
Whoa!

15
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:25,400
Oh, crap! Can you get me some tissues?

16
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:26,503
It's empty.

17
00:01:26,503 --> 00:01:29,170
Sorry, there's more in my bedroom closet.

18
00:01:29,170 --> 00:01:30,290
Okay.

19
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:32,580
This is bad...

20
00:01:34,090 --> 00:01:36,370
Man, this...

21
00:01:36,970 --> 00:01:40,270
It's going to smell like strawberry...

22
00:01:58,440 --> 00:01:59,960
Yum!

23
00:02:00,650 --> 00:02:03,150
I might have invented something.

24
00:02:03,150 --> 00:02:05,130
Double syrup is the best.

25
00:02:07,740 --> 00:02:09,470
Did you know?

26
00:02:09,470 --> 00:02:13,250
Apparently all shaved ice syrups
taste the same.

27
00:02:13,250 --> 00:02:16,270
Huh? Really?

28
00:02:16,270 --> 00:02:18,880
Strawberry, lemon, blue Hawaii...

29
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:21,310
They're all the same sweetener.

30
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:31,440
But it's strawberry and lemon...

31
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:35,510
Apparently the scent and color
create the illusion of taste.

32
00:02:35,510 --> 00:02:38,690
In the end, people prioritize what they see.

33
00:02:40,110 --> 00:02:42,420
I kind of feel tricked.

34
00:02:46,830 --> 00:02:50,310
By the way, why a double?

35
00:02:50,310 --> 00:02:53,150
What? The syrup?

36
00:02:53,150 --> 00:02:54,710
The bed.

37
00:02:58,080 --> 00:02:59,490
Is that bad?

38
00:03:00,490 --> 00:03:04,400
No, but it was a little surprising.

39
00:03:04,990 --> 00:03:10,610
You must've been pretty confident,
expecting us to get together like that.

40
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:16,580
It was like making a wish.

41
00:03:16,580 --> 00:03:18,630
And it came true right away.

42
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:22,980
A wish?

43
00:03:24,310 --> 00:03:27,470
A wish for you to come here.

44
00:03:33,141 --> 00:03:35,141
Oh, sorry.

45
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:43,235
[Shoko Hagiwara]

46
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:46,370
Gonna answer?

47
00:03:46,370 --> 00:03:48,900
It's fine. I'll call back later.

48
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:52,850
Answer it. It might be urgent.

49
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:58,320
Hello?

50
00:04:03,670 --> 00:04:07,560
<i>Hey, you're not coming home for Obon?</i>

51
00:04:08,430 --> 00:04:10,760
I'm busy with this and that.

52
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:13,980
<i>Busy? When you don't even have a girlfriend?</i>

53
00:04:15,550 --> 00:04:17,570
It's work.

54
00:04:17,570 --> 00:04:20,820
I was looking forward to seeing Kaori...

55
00:04:22,590 --> 00:04:25,440
Stop bringing that up.

56
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:29,320
Give marriage and the future
some more thought, okay?

57
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:32,410
<i>I'm busy now. I'll contact you later.</i>

58
00:04:32,410 --> 00:04:33,850
Wait!

59
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:03,470
What are you looking at?

60
00:05:03,470 --> 00:05:05,750
I hear a festival.

61
00:05:05,750 --> 00:05:07,170
A festival?

62
00:05:16,330 --> 00:05:17,810
You're right.

63
00:06:17,900 --> 00:06:19,938
I'm hungry.

64
00:06:20,794 --> 00:06:22,299
Let's eat here.

65
00:06:22,299 --> 00:06:23,592
Nice.

66
00:06:26,094 --> 00:06:30,350
So, I, Adachi, am getting married.

67
00:06:30,350 --> 00:06:32,880
- Huh?
- Huh? With who?

68
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:34,730
With who?

69
00:06:34,730 --> 00:06:37,980
Obviously, the person I'm currently dating.

70
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:42,460
Well, it feels like you prefer
girls you met three days ago.

71
00:06:42,460 --> 00:06:45,010
Stop. You make me sound crazy.

72
00:06:45,010 --> 00:06:46,590
No, I kind of get it.

73
00:06:46,590 --> 00:06:49,580
I didn't expect you
to get married for a while.

74
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:53,200
Well, that was the plan, but...

75
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:56,650
Could it be...

76
00:06:56,650 --> 00:07:00,390
We're having a baby.

77
00:07:00,390 --> 00:07:02,980
- Seriously?
- Wow, congratulations!

78
00:07:02,980 --> 00:07:04,490
That's amazing.

79
00:07:04,490 --> 00:07:07,177
Dang, I'm shocked.

80
00:07:07,177 --> 00:07:09,620
It's Nakarai. Nakarai!

81
00:07:09,620 --> 00:07:12,340
Hurry! Faster, faster!

82
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:14,340
Get over here!

83
00:07:17,042 --> 00:07:19,024
Your order is here.

84
00:07:22,090 --> 00:07:24,510
Lunch? Let's eat together.

85
00:07:24,510 --> 00:07:26,160
No, I'm just getting coffee.

86
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:28,930
Come on, just drink it here with us.

87
00:07:32,510 --> 00:07:35,720
Adachi's getting married.

88
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,625
- Oh, congrats.
- Thanks.

89
00:07:37,625 --> 00:07:39,260
So he's done being a playboy then?

90
00:07:39,260 --> 00:07:43,030
Come on, not you too!
Just who do you think I am?

91
00:07:43,030 --> 00:07:45,810
Still, you're getting married so fast...

92
00:07:45,810 --> 00:07:48,710
Did you hear?
Our co-worker Moriya's marrying too.

93
00:07:48,710 --> 00:07:51,370
Hagiwara's planning the after-party again.

94
00:07:51,370 --> 00:07:53,060
Yeah, that's right.

95
00:07:53,060 --> 00:07:54,960
Excuse me.

96
00:07:59,229 --> 00:08:01,099
I ordered too much.

97
00:08:03,170 --> 00:08:04,840
Hagiwara!

98
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:07,320
Hey, you're eating lunch here?

99
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:09,810
Shigeta! What a coincidence.

100
00:08:09,810 --> 00:08:12,880
I'm the one who taught you to slack off here.

101
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:14,760
Did you?

102
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:17,990
Hey, you broke up
with your girlfriend, right?

103
00:08:19,310 --> 00:08:22,420
Want me to introduce you to someone next?

104
00:08:22,420 --> 00:08:24,070
No thanks, I don't need that.

105
00:08:24,070 --> 00:08:27,080
Hey, don't be shy.

106
00:08:34,830 --> 00:08:40,140
Hello, this is Shigeta.
Yes, thank you for the call.

107
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:42,820
Yes, thank you very much.

108
00:08:42,820 --> 00:08:46,090
Right, yes...

109
00:08:48,290 --> 00:08:50,460
That was lucky.

110
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:54,990
I'm heading back.

111
00:08:54,990 --> 00:08:56,200
Okay.

112
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:36,320
[Summer Festival]

113
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:37,718
[Request for Funding]

114
00:09:37,718 --> 00:09:40,706
[Seeking individuals and companies
to support and sponsor the festival.]

115
00:09:40,706 --> 00:09:41,996
[Call or visit to apply.]

116
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:19,607
Welcome.

117
00:10:19,607 --> 00:10:21,470
Please come in.

118
00:10:32,420 --> 00:10:34,100
I'll have today's wine.

119
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:35,260
Sure.

120
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:36,310
Me too then.

121
00:10:36,310 --> 00:10:37,970
Okay.

122
00:10:37,970 --> 00:10:39,940
I haven't had dinner.

123
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:43,560
I'll have the salmon pâté
and whatever you recommend.

124
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:46,070
Yes, coming right up.

125
00:10:54,650 --> 00:10:56,800
Do you come here often?

126
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:58,680
Sometimes.

127
00:10:58,680 --> 00:11:02,350
They're open late,
so it's convenient if I work overtime.

128
00:11:02,350 --> 00:11:03,970
I see...

129
00:11:10,690 --> 00:11:12,230
What?

130
00:11:12,890 --> 00:11:14,360
Are you still mad?

131
00:11:14,360 --> 00:11:15,800
About what?

132
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:18,590
About Shigeta at lunch today.

133
00:11:21,730 --> 00:11:24,270
He has some strong quirks,

134
00:11:24,270 --> 00:11:27,680
but he's a really good senior to me.

135
00:11:27,680 --> 00:11:30,790
Mentors can mean a lot, you know?

136
00:11:30,790 --> 00:11:33,080
Don't you have one too?

137
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:37,340
Mine was a female senior, so not especially.

138
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:40,120
And that's not my vibe anyway.

139
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:44,820
It's not like I chose a male senior
because I wanted to.

140
00:11:50,170 --> 00:11:52,180
True.

141
00:11:52,180 --> 00:11:53,690
That's how it usually is.

142
00:11:53,690 --> 00:11:55,980
Wait, why are you saying it like that?

143
00:11:55,980 --> 00:11:57,800
Like what?

144
00:12:01,150 --> 00:12:02,960
Here you go.

145
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:04,340
Thanks.

146
00:12:09,170 --> 00:12:12,280
This is the first time
you've brought a friend, Nakarai.

147
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:13,940
Is he from work?

148
00:12:13,940 --> 00:12:15,720
Yes.

149
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:19,570
You never come on weekends, Nakarai.

150
00:12:19,570 --> 00:12:21,070
Because it looks crowded.

151
00:12:21,070 --> 00:12:23,000
No, not at all.

152
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,780
Please come visit.

153
00:12:24,780 --> 00:12:26,020
I'll drop by sometime.

154
00:12:26,020 --> 00:12:27,350
Okay.

155
00:12:29,850 --> 00:12:32,520
Your friend is handsome.

156
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:34,890
Does he have a girlfriend?

157
00:12:34,890 --> 00:12:36,250
Someone I'm dating?

158
00:12:36,250 --> 00:12:37,540
Yes.

159
00:12:40,580 --> 00:12:42,310
Well, of course I do.

160
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:46,930
Wow, I'm jealous.

161
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:52,070
I'm desperate for a boyfriend right now.

162
00:12:54,670 --> 00:12:56,970
Introduce me to someone.

163
00:12:58,090 --> 00:12:59,790
I'm rooting for you.

164
00:13:00,390 --> 00:13:05,230
Ayuko, tell them to bake the baguette
a little crispier than usual.

165
00:13:06,870 --> 00:13:11,140
Okay. Manager, bread extra crispy.

166
00:13:31,820 --> 00:13:34,350
You shouldn't be like that.

167
00:13:34,350 --> 00:13:35,420
What?

168
00:13:35,420 --> 00:13:38,940
That girl is clearly
interested in you, Nakarai.

169
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:41,560
Why would you bring me there?

170
00:13:41,560 --> 00:13:42,860
You noticed?

171
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:44,710
Of course I noticed.

172
00:13:45,780 --> 00:13:48,750
It's not like there's any real harm.

173
00:13:48,750 --> 00:13:53,080
Just so you know, I haven't done anything
to make her misunderstand.

174
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:55,200
You used her name.

175
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:57,470
Didn't you look at the menu?

176
00:13:57,470 --> 00:14:01,220
It says "Ayuko's homemade dessert
of the day".

177
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:04,160
So asking her last name would be rude.

178
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:13,920
I wonder why we're so upset.

179
00:14:15,310 --> 00:14:20,090
Well... in my case, it's jealousy.

180
00:14:27,550 --> 00:14:28,750
Here.

181
00:14:29,580 --> 00:14:31,410
What is it?

182
00:14:31,410 --> 00:14:35,220
Your lips are dry, even though it's summer.

183
00:14:35,220 --> 00:14:36,680
Ah...

184
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:41,600
Put it on. Put it on for me, Nakarai.

185
00:14:44,050 --> 00:14:45,870
If you say so.

186
00:14:52,010 --> 00:14:53,770
Don't move.

187
00:14:59,190 --> 00:15:02,040
There's such a strong honey feel.

188
00:15:02,040 --> 00:15:05,820
I got it today. A souvenir from Taiwan.

189
00:15:07,090 --> 00:15:09,820
It might attract ants.

190
00:15:09,820 --> 00:15:12,290
I'll get to you before the ants.

191
00:15:14,020 --> 00:15:15,594
You know, Nakarai...

192
00:15:17,020 --> 00:15:20,240
You're surprisingly good at this.
Does it come naturally?

193
00:15:21,170 --> 00:15:23,870
It's because you're so cute.

194
00:15:24,970 --> 00:15:26,660
You're annoying.

195
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:59,370
Oh, man. I want to go home soon.

196
00:15:59,370 --> 00:16:02,180
I wish we could just teleport there.

197
00:16:03,710 --> 00:16:06,520
You're so cute when you're like this.

198
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:45,200
Don't look. It's embarrassing.

199
00:16:46,430 --> 00:16:49,610
Treat me today, okay?

200
00:16:49,610 --> 00:16:51,090
Huh?

201
00:16:51,090 --> 00:16:52,890
Treat me.

202
00:16:52,890 --> 00:16:56,050
Sure, but... what exactly?

203
00:17:18,850 --> 00:17:22,790
Treat you here? Why?

204
00:17:22,790 --> 00:17:25,336
Because I paid for you without asking.

205
00:17:25,336 --> 00:17:27,080
Paid for what?

206
00:17:27,080 --> 00:17:29,260
Funding for the festival.

207
00:17:30,860 --> 00:17:33,000
Sorry, what do you mean?

208
00:17:43,330 --> 00:17:48,060
The other day, I saw a flyer
for this festival in the shopping arcade.

209
00:17:48,060 --> 00:17:49,840
I like this kind of thing.

210
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:51,620
Oh, is that so?

211
00:17:51,620 --> 00:17:57,020
Small festivals and rituals
that would never bring in tourists.

212
00:18:01,650 --> 00:18:03,770
- Here you go.
- Thanks.

213
00:18:07,190 --> 00:18:11,790
It feels like all sorts of things
are being preserved here.

214
00:18:14,720 --> 00:18:16,010
Yeah.

215
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:20,140
So I donated money.

216
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:24,400
5,000 yen each, in your name and mine.

217
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:26,160
Oh?

218
00:18:35,197 --> 00:18:36,617
It fell off.

219
00:18:40,030 --> 00:18:41,720
Whoa.

220
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:44,050
- For you.
- Thanks.

221
00:18:46,660 --> 00:18:48,370
Yum!

222
00:18:48,370 --> 00:18:50,020
The coffee's great.

223
00:18:50,020 --> 00:18:52,010
Let's make this with Mr. Penguin.

224
00:18:52,010 --> 00:18:54,110
We'll need condensed milk.

225
00:19:00,265 --> 00:19:02,525
Hey, do you see that?

226
00:19:03,700 --> 00:19:05,510
I know right?

227
00:19:05,510 --> 00:19:08,370
- That cotton candy looks good.
- Yeah, it does.

228
00:19:08,370 --> 00:19:09,733
- Want some?
- Yeah.

229
00:19:09,733 --> 00:19:11,113
Let's go.

230
00:19:31,590 --> 00:19:34,665
What happens to these after they float down?

231
00:19:34,665 --> 00:19:36,458
[Place messages and offerings to the deceased
and your ancestors]

232
00:19:36,458 --> 00:19:38,250
[to drift down the river with your feelings]

233
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:42,850
They probably collect them somewhere, right?

234
00:19:42,850 --> 00:19:46,230
It'd probably be bad
if they just go out to sea.

235
00:19:46,230 --> 00:19:48,908
It'd be illegal dumping.

236
00:19:48,908 --> 00:19:51,508
Sounds weird when you say it though.

237
00:19:53,560 --> 00:19:58,450
So in the end, they can't go anywhere.

238
00:20:05,770 --> 00:20:07,230
Want to go see?

239
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:10,550
It's fine.

240
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:37,230
Oh, this is...

241
00:20:37,230 --> 00:20:38,740
There it is.

242
00:20:40,030 --> 00:20:41,198
You're right.

243
00:20:41,198 --> 00:20:43,110
[Sei Nakarai]
[Kazuaki Hagiwara]

244
00:20:43,110 --> 00:20:46,290
Hagiwara, notice anything?

245
00:20:46,290 --> 00:20:47,750
Yeah, there it is.

246
00:20:47,750 --> 00:20:49,670
Not that.

247
00:20:50,460 --> 00:20:52,440
Huh?

248
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:55,800
I'm talking about why our names are there.

249
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:58,630
Because you paid for both of us?

250
00:20:58,630 --> 00:21:00,719
No, look closely.

251
00:21:00,719 --> 00:21:02,620
It's in alphabetic order.

252
00:21:03,209 --> 00:21:05,284
Aida... Ao...

253
00:21:07,626 --> 00:21:13,177
[Hirose... Hirata... Nakarai... Hagiwara]

254
00:21:13,860 --> 00:21:15,930
You're right.

255
00:21:15,930 --> 00:21:19,080
Huh? Then why are we
right next to each other?

256
00:21:19,080 --> 00:21:22,680
Because I submitted my name as "Han'i".
(*Nakarai can be pronounced as Han'i)

257
00:21:22,680 --> 00:21:26,250
That's why I'm right next to Hagiwara.

258
00:21:26,250 --> 00:21:29,250
I checked online. It's a real name.

259
00:21:29,250 --> 00:21:30,420
Why?

260
00:21:30,420 --> 00:21:34,270
Why? I just wanted
to see us lined up together.

261
00:21:37,270 --> 00:21:42,110
Good thing there weren't any
Hanyus or Hamadas.

262
00:21:53,030 --> 00:21:55,510
Let's go to the sea next time.

263
00:21:55,510 --> 00:21:58,070
Next year and the year after too.

264
00:21:58,960 --> 00:22:00,630
Why every year?

265
00:22:01,550 --> 00:22:02,940
No reason.

266
00:22:26,430 --> 00:22:28,125
What's your wish?

267
00:22:30,766 --> 00:22:32,186
It's a secret.

268
00:22:32,936 --> 00:22:34,586
I see.

269
00:22:36,330 --> 00:22:37,730
Hagiwara.

270
00:22:38,750 --> 00:22:42,830
It's a shrine, so you bow twice,
clap twice, and bow once.

271
00:22:42,830 --> 00:22:45,300
I know that much.

272
00:22:45,300 --> 00:22:46,540
I thought you didn't know.

273
00:22:46,540 --> 00:22:48,550
I know.

274
00:23:00,640 --> 00:23:04,100
What does the after-party organizer
for a wedding actually do?

275
00:23:04,100 --> 00:23:06,570
They said they'll let us
take care of everything.

276
00:23:06,570 --> 00:23:08,042
"Us"?

277
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:13,240
Look at my phone anytime.

278
00:23:13,240 --> 00:23:15,390
- I'm not gonna worry.
- Come on, worry a little.

279
00:23:15,390 --> 00:23:18,070
Jeez, it's fine.
Why do you want me to distrust you?

280
00:23:18,070 --> 00:23:19,380
Sorry.

281
00:23:19,380 --> 00:23:21,050
I can't come over tonight anymore.

282
00:23:21,050 --> 00:23:22,550
Are you alone today?

283
00:23:22,550 --> 00:23:24,780
Don't you have something to say?

284
00:23:24,780 --> 00:23:27,170
I have something to say to you.

285
00:23:27,170 --> 00:23:28,190
You do?

286
00:23:28,190 --> 00:23:31,177
It started with an email.

287
00:23:31,177 --> 00:23:32,990
That's exactly why...

288
00:23:32,990 --> 00:23:36,040
Because I don't want
to regret falling for him.

289
00:23:36,040 --> 00:23:39,150
Even after I fell for you,
I kept my guard up.

290
00:23:39,150 --> 00:23:42,130
And yet, every little thing you said and did
had me up and down.

291
00:23:42,130 --> 00:23:45,120
We never had that kind of thing, right?

292
00:23:45,120 --> 00:23:49,620
So, after I fell in love,
I fell in love again.

293
00:23:49,620 --> 00:23:51,020
You're finally back.

294
00:23:51,020 --> 00:23:52,220
Why are you laughing?

295
00:23:52,220 --> 00:23:54,030
They're leaning on each other.

296
00:23:54,030 --> 00:23:55,900
Yeah, they're well-made.

297
00:23:55,900 --> 00:23:57,410
Cheers.

298
00:23:57,410 --> 00:23:58,740
Cheers.
